# Generated by `make test-savings`: the numbers change on every run, so the file
# is an output rather than a source. It stays on disk after the run.
tests/token_savings_report.md

# Local planning scratch. `plan/*` rather than `plan/` so that a single
# subdirectory can be exempted below: git will not re-include anything inside an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so the exemption has to start one level up.
plan/*
# …except the rules, which are cited from a lot of places that a fresh clone
# has to be able to follow — CONTRIBUTING links plan/rules/code_rules.md, and
# ~40 source comments point at it and at relation_contract.md by name.
!plan/rules/
# The scheduler cites this one by section number from five source files
# (chunk_plan.rs "§5", chunk_queue.rs "§4, §6", chunk_queue_ops.rs "§8", …), so
# it has to be in the repo for those references to mean anything. Same two-step
# as above: the directory has to be re-included before a file inside it can be,
# which is why `!plan/next/` comes before `plan/next/*`.
!plan/next/
plan/next/*
!plan/next/DYNAMIC_SCHED_REDESIGN.md

